{"name":"Clown Nose","hex":"#e94257","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"clown nose","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fake nose, typically near spherical, bright red in color and sometimes capable of producing a honking sound when squeezed, commonly used by clowns and occasionally as a prop by people during parties.","A reddish-brown cancerous bulge in the area of the tip of the nose."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clown_nose"}],"entries":[{"title":"Clown","blocks":[{"text":"A clown is a person who performs physical comedy and arts in an open-ended fashion, typically while wearing distinct makeup or costuming and reversing folkway-norms. The art of performing as a clown is known as clowning or buffoonery, and the term \"clown\" may be used synonymously with predecessors like jester, joker, buffoon, fool, or harlequin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Auguste_clown_reading_a_book_upside-down.jpg/330px-Auguste_clown_reading_a_book_upside-down.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clown","wikidata":"Q7358"},{"title":"Nose","blocks":[{"text":"A nose is a sensory organ and respiratory structure in vertebrates. It consists of a nasal cavity inside the head, and an external nose on the face. The external nose houses the nostrils, or nares, a pair of tubes providing airflow through the nose for respiration. Where the nostrils pass through the nasal cavity they widen, are known as nasal fossae, and contain turbinates and olfactory mucosa. The nasal cavity also connects to the paranasal sinuses. From the nasal cavity, the nostrils continue into the pharynx, a switch track valve connecting the respiratory and digestive systems."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Canine_Nose_Macro_Photo.png/330px-Canine_Nose_Macro_Photo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nose","wikidata":"Q7363"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Joseph_Grimaldi.jpg/500px-Joseph_Grimaldi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Joseph_Grimaldi.jpg/500px-Joseph_Grimaldi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Joseph Grimaldi as \"Joey\" the Clown, c. 1810","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJoseph_Grimaldi.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/LES_ROSSYANN_Weisscloun_und_dummer_August.JPG/500px-LES_ROSSYANN_Weisscloun_und_dummer_August.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/LES_ROSSYANN_Weisscloun_und_dummer_August.JPG/500px-LES_ROSSYANN_Weisscloun_und_dummer_August.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Les Rossyann, white clown and clumsy Auguste from France","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALES_ROSSYANN_Weisscloun_und_dummer_August.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/G.L._Fox_the_original_Humpty_Dumpty._LCCN2014635786.jpg/500px-G.L._Fox_the_original_Humpty_Dumpty._LCCN2014635786.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/G.L._Fox_the_original_Humpty_Dumpty._LCCN2014635786.jpg/1280px-G.L._Fox_the_original_Humpty_Dumpty._LCCN2014635786.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/G.L._Fox_the_original_Humpty_Dumpty._LCCN2014635786.jpg/500px-G.L._Fox_the_original_Humpty_Dumpty._LCCN2014635786.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"G.L. Fox, the original Hum